# Plan Frontmatter + Archival Discipline

SSOT: `unified-trading-pm/plans/PLAN_FORMAT.md` (frontmatter schema) +
`/codex/12-agent-workflow/plan-completion-and-archival-discipline.md` (archival ritual).

> **RETIRED 2026-08-02**: the `completion_gates`/`repo_gates`/`type`/`epic` 3-tier C/D/B gate model this rule used to
> describe is the LEGACY pre-2026-05-21 schema — `plans/PLAN_FORMAT.md`'s own Archive Criteria section rules "no
> current plan carries those fields, so no plan could ever satisfy it." Do NOT add these fields to a new plan.

## RULE: Required YAML Fields (current schema)

Every plan/issue doc carries the universal-core fields: `doc_type`, `title`, `summary`, `status`, `nature`,
`asset_group`, `stage`, `repos`, `scope`, `tags`, `related`, `created`, `parent_epic`, `assigned_vm`,
`execution_scope`, `priority`, `estimate_class`, `estimate_baseline`/`calibrated_ai_days`, `assigned_role`,
`drift_direction` — plus optional `depends_on`, `locked_by`/`since`, `supersedes`/`superseded_by`, `source`. Full
schema + closed-vocab enums: `/codex/11-project-management/doc-frontmatter-schema.md`.

`assigned_vm` ∈ `{planning, NA}` only — `planning` = agent-orchestrator VM dispatches it; `NA` = not auto-dispatched
(operator-driven). `status: draft` = WIP, NOT ingested by the backlog; flip to `active` to dispatch.

Missing a required field is a plan format violation — fix before committing (enforced by
`scripts/plan-hygiene/check_frontmatter_schema.py`).

## RULE: ai/ vs active/ Split

- AI-generated drafts not yet reviewed → `plans/ai/`
- User-approved / operator-authored plans → `plans/active/` (current frontmatter schema above)

## RULE: Archive Eligibility

A plan with EVERY todo done (`- [x]`) and unlocked (no `locked_by:`) MUST be archived immediately — don't leave it
sitting `active`. `locked_by:` blocks archival without an explicit `[unlock-plan]` (ask the operator, never
autonomous). Full archival ritual (incl. the fact-vs-path referrer rule):
`/codex/12-agent-workflow/plan-completion-and-archival-discipline.md`.

NEVER mark a plan done/archived while any todo is still `- [ ]` — partial completion is not archive-eligible.

## RULE: blocked_by / depends_on in Todos

When a plan is blocked by another plan's incomplete work, use `blocked_by: <plan-slug>` on the specific todo item, or
`depends_on:` in frontmatter for a whole-plan prerequisite. External dependencies belong in todos/frontmatter, not an
invented gate field.

## RULE: New Plans from AI Sessions

When any agent (Claude Code, Cursor, GHA autonomous) generates a new plan:
1. **ASK BEFORE CREATING (HARD RULE)**: agent-orchestrator plan (`assigned_vm: planning`) or human plan
   (`assigned_vm: NA`)? Default is human unless the operator explicitly says otherwise.
2. Author directly in `plans/active/` with the current frontmatter schema (see above), or `plans/ai/` if genuinely a
   draft awaiting review before promotion.

## WHY This Matters

Plans were previously archived when most todos were done, ignoring the todos still open. Every follow-up is a
tracked `- [ ]` todo, never prose. A plan with every todo done + unlocked must be archived immediately — don't leave
stale `active` plans cluttering the corpus (orphan count > 0 is review-blocking, per
`scripts/plan-hygiene/regenerate_active_plan_inventory.py`).

